+4.  **Lighting Integration (Optional):** To apply lighting, first render the surface normals into an image-like map as described in Step 3 [S1, unofficial]. Then, use a diffuse lighting function (e.g., `PyTorch3D.renderer.lighting`) to compute the brightness under a point light source using the rendered normals and a predefined light position [S1, unofficial].
 
